    {
      "name": "03 Flow and explanation",
      "view": "flowchart",
      "role": "notes",
      "title": "RAG assistant | Flow and explanation",
      "titleFontSize": 23,
      "subtitle": "PAGE 1 ONLY | Native process cards explain the main workload; no proposed architecture is added here.",
      "width": 18,
      "height": 11,
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "flow-step-1",
          "kind": "card",
          "cardStyle": "detail",
          "label": "01  Prepare the knowledge corpus\nIngestion code reads approved blobs, divides document text into manageable chunks, calls Azure OpenAI for document embeddings and writes chunks, source identifiers and vectors into Azure AI Search. This preparation runs independently of an individual interactive question.",
          "x": 5.0,
          "y": 8.75,
          "width": 8.5,
          "height": 1.4,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "color": "RGB(148,163,184)",
          "fill": "RGB(255,255,255)",
          "mainNodeIds": [
            "rag-docs",
            "rag-ingest",
            "rag-ai",
            "rag-search"
          ],
          "mainEdgeIds": [
            "rag-read-documents",
            "rag-embeddings",
            "rag-index"
          ],
          "state": "MAIN explanation"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-step-2",
          "kind": "card",
          "cardStyle": "detail",
          "label": "02  Accept a question and retrieve\nThe user submits a question to the App Service application. Application code queries the existing search index for candidate evidence. The main view assumes text retrieval; storing document vectors does not automatically enable or select a vector-query strategy.",
          "x": 5.0,
          "y": 7.05,
          "width": 8.5,
          "height": 1.4,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "color": "RGB(148,163,184)",
          "fill": "RGB(255,255,255)",
          "mainNodeIds": [
            "questioner",
            "rag-app",
            "rag-search"
          ],
          "mainEdgeIds": [
            "rag-question",
            "rag-retrieval"
          ],
          "state": "MAIN explanation"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-step-3",
          "kind": "card",
          "cardStyle": "detail",
          "label": "03  Decide whether evidence is adequate\nApplication logic checks whether the retrieved material is relevant and permitted for this user. Missing or inadequate evidence follows the no-evidence branch. This is a required application decision, not a promise that the model reliably detects every unsupported statement.",
          "x": 5.0,
          "y": 5.35,
          "width": 8.5,
          "height": 1.4,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "color": "RGB(148,163,184)",
          "fill": "RGB(255,255,255)",
          "mainNodeIds": [
            "rag-app",
            "rag-search"
          ],
          "mainEdgeIds": [
            "rag-retrieval"
          ],
          "state": "MAIN explanation"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-step-4",
          "kind": "card",
          "cardStyle": "detail",
          "label": "04  Generate a grounded draft\nFor an answerable question, the application sends the question and selected evidence to Azure OpenAI. The model returns a draft answer. Prompt construction, content checks and source attribution belong to the application; retrieval alone does not prove factual correctness.",
          "x": 5.0,
          "y": 3.65,
          "width": 8.5,
          "height": 1.4,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "color": "RGB(148,163,184)",
          "fill": "RGB(255,255,255)",
          "mainNodeIds": [
            "rag-app",
            "rag-ai"
          ],
          "mainEdgeIds": [
            "rag-generation"
          ],
          "state": "MAIN explanation"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-step-5",
          "kind": "card",
          "cardStyle": "detail",
          "label": "05  Return an answer or abstention\nThe assistant returns an answer with source references when evidence and checks permit, or an explicit abstention when they do not. The response returns to the same user channel. Document ingestion is not repeated merely because a question was asked.",
          "x": 5.0,
          "y": 1.95,
          "width": 8.5,
          "height": 1.4,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "color": "RGB(148,163,184)",
          "fill": "RGB(255,255,255)",
          "mainNodeIds": [
            "questioner",
            "rag-app"
          ],
          "mainEdgeIds": [
            "rag-question"
          ],
          "state": "MAIN explanation"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-prose-1",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "MAIN design in plain language\n\nThere are two rhythms on page 1: preparing the corpus and answering a question. Functions owns custom ingestion, Blob Storage holds the source material, AI Search holds searchable chunks, and Azure OpenAI serves model calls. App Service orchestrates user requests. No managed agent framework, external web search or automatic document parser is silently inserted. The first flow step summarizes ingestion prerequisites rather than a per-question transaction.",
          "x": 14.0,
          "y": 8.05,
          "width": 6.2,
          "height": 2.65,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fill": "RGB(245,248,252)"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-prose-2",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "Assumptions and service caveats\n\nOnly approved synthetic text documents are assumed. Scanned PDFs, document extraction, index refresh policy, embedding dimensions and model deployments remain choices. Public endpoints are the baseline; hosting tiers and network support are not selected. Model availability, capacity and quotas vary by deployment and region. AI Search configuration must match the application's retrieval strategy. Neither a service icon nor an embedding guarantees authorization or answer quality.",
          "x": 14.0,
          "y": 5.15,
          "width": 6.2,
          "height": 2.65,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fill": "RGB(245,248,252)"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow-prose-3",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "What requires validation\n\nValidate source permissions, freshness, answer grounding, prompt-injection handling and safe logging before broader use. Test missing evidence, stale indexes, throttling and unavailable models; a retry must respect service limits. The visible branch returns an abstention without an unnecessary generation call. This explanation covers page 1 only and does not import the separate hardening proposal. No production, compliance or confidential-data handling assurance is asserted.",
          "x": 14.0,
          "y": 2.25,
          "width": 6.2,
          "height": 2.65,
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fill": "RGB(245,248,252)"
        }
      ],
